window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-kushida-kikyou"]=[{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou","q":"entrance ceremony bus  the public champion crowded city bus heading to anhs on entrance ceremony morning  an elderly woman is standing in the aisle  unsteady on her feet  an office lady scolds koenji first  most passengers look away or pretend not to notice   um  i think that the lady is right   unexpected support  delivered brave and frank   this poor woman appears to have been suffering for quite some time now  won t you offer up your seat  while you might consider such courtesy unnecessary  i think it would contribute greatly to society   everyone  please listen to me for just a moment  won t someone give up their seat for this woman  it doesn t matter who  please","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Entrance ceremony bus: the public champion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.19–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crowded city bus heading to ANHS on entrance ceremony morning. An elderly woman is standing in the aisle, unsteady on her feet. An office lady scolds Kōenji first; most passengers look away or pretend not to notice.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Um… I think that the lady is right.” (unexpected support, delivered brave and frank)<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This poor woman appears to have been suffering for quite some time now. Won’t you offer up your seat? While you might consider such courtesy unnecessary, I think it would contribute greatly to society.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, please listen to me for just a moment. Won’t someone give up their seat for this woman? It doesn’t matter who. Please.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> An unnamed girl wearing the ANHS uniform — the text never names her here, but she is the one later understood to be Kushida (see [note]) — steps forward from the aisle and directly faces Kōenji, who is lounging in the priority seating.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Kōenji haughtily refuses and declares he cares only for his own satisfaction, she refuses to back down or accept defeat. Instead of retreating, she turns to face the entire crowded bus without fear.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Extraordinary social courage and charisma; her appeal moves an office lady to stand and surrender her seat out of guilt (“E-excuse me. You can have mine.”), settling the matter.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Earnest, pleading, gentle, highly moral public register that commands collective attention without sounding aggressive.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Direct moral clash; attempts to appeal to social conscience against his absolute solipsism.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bus text never names the uniformed challenger. Her identification with Kushida is an inference (she later knows AK and Horikita spoke at the gate that day, p.57), not a stated fact in Year 1, Vol. 1.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\">→ After: Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"classroom day 1  empathetic rescue   friendship declaration class 1 d classroom after homeroom orientation  hirata asks students to introduce themselves from the front row   it s okay to go slowly  don t rush   my name is kushida kikyou  none of my friends from junior high made it to this school  so i m alone here  i d like to get to know all of your names and faces right away and become friends as soon as possible   my first goal is to become friends with everyone  so  after we re finished with introductions  i d love for you to share your contact information with me   so  after school or during vacations  i want to make all sorts of memories with lots of people  please feel free to invite me to lots and lots of events  anyway  i ve talked for a long time  so i ll end my introduction here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.34–35<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after homeroom orientation. Hirata asks students to introduce themselves from the front row.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s okay to go slowly. Don’t rush.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name is Kushida Kikyou. None of my friends from junior high made it to this school, so I’m alone here. I’d like to get to know all of your names and faces right away and become friends as soon as possible!”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My first goal is to become friends with everyone. So, after we’re finished with introductions, I’d love for you to share your contact information with me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Established as the idol and social anchor of Class 1-D.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Inogashira Kokoro freezes at her desk, trembling and pale. Classmates mistakenly shout “Do your best!” which heightens her panic. Kushida steps in with immediate, emotionally intelligent guidance.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Instinctive social psychology: understands that “Do your best!” applies forceful pressure, whereas “Just take things slowly. Don’t rush,” removes urgency and restores calm. Inogashira successfully finishes her intro.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps up cheerfully as the next speaker, glowing with approachable energy.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, after school or during vacations, I want to make all sorts of memories with lots of people. Please feel free to invite me to lots and lots of events! Anyway, I’ve talked for a long time, so I’ll end my introduction here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Outward persona: boundless warmth, radical accessibility, open-hearted desire to unite the entire class and befriend every student without distinction.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Instantly established as the undisputed idol and social anchor of Class 1-D.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1\">← Before: Entrance ceremony bus: the public champion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\">→ After: Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"corridor interception  probing for horikita s secrets on ayanokoji s way out of the classroom at lunch on day 2  he d resolved to eat alone  kushida approaches him with a radiant smile  holding something he can t identify   possibly a pouch covered in key holders   i m kushida  from your class  do you remember me  she asked   to tell you the truth  there s something i wanted to ask you  it s just one little question  ayanokouji kun  are you on good terms with horikita san   oh  no  well  do you remember when i said i wanted to get along with everyone in class  that s why i wanted everyone s contact info  but  horikita turned me down   i was just wondering what kind of person horikita san is   kushida continued   is she the type who ll talk a lot when she s with a friend   well  during our introductions  horikita san walked out of the classroom  right  it seems like she hasn t talked to anybody yet  so i m a little worried about her   hmm  i see  i thought that you two must have been old friends before starting school here  i m sorry to have asked you such a strange question   how  you introduced yourself the other day  didn t you  i remembered   she d listened to his hopelessly lame self introduction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.56–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On Ayanokōji’s way out of the classroom at lunch on Day 2 (he’d resolved to eat alone). Kushida approaches him with a radiant smile, holding something he can’t identify — possibly a pouch covered in key holders.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m Kushida, from your class. Do you remember me?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“To tell you the truth, there’s something I wanted to ask you. It’s just one little question. Ayanokouji-kun, are you on good terms with Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, no. Well, do you remember when I said I wanted to get along with everyone in class? That’s why I wanted everyone’s contact info. But… Horikita turned me down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls out to him cheerfully (“You’re Ayanokouji-kun, right?”); Ayanokōji’s heart pounds like a jackhammer at her beauty (short, straight dyed-brown hair, one of the newly approved short skirt lengths).<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When he says he barely knows Horikita, she pivots to probing what kind of person she is, then frames her interest as pointed “worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just wondering what kind of person Horikita-san is,” (Kushida continued)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is she the type who’ll talk a lot when she’s with a friend?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, during our introductions, Horikita-san walked out of the classroom, right? It seems like she hasn’t talked to anybody yet, so I’m a little worried about her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. I see. I thought that you two must have been old friends before starting school here. I’m sorry to have asked you such a strange question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How? You introduced yourself the other day, didn’t you? I remembered.” (she’d listened to his hopelessly lame self-introduction)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes with a radiant handshake: “Well, it’s nice to meet you again, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Relentless social campaigner; frames investigative probing as friendly concern; remembers even the least remarkable classmates’ introductions; warmth weaponized as an information-gathering tool.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Bubbly, innocent, persistently encouraging, masking an unyielding determination.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Fixation begins: determined to break through Horikita’s barriers; encodes her as the girl who refused contact info and “hasn’t talked to anybody yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recruits him as her bridge and information source to reach Horikita; establishes their first warm real-world contact (handshake).<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\">→ After: Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"swim heat   detecting ayanokoji s physique indoor swimming pool   i m really looking forward to this  both kouejin kun and sudou kun are so fast   corpus renders koenji s name as  kouejin kun  here   kept verbatim   hmm  what s the matter  your face looks red for some reason  are you not feeling well  by chance   you re much faster than average  too  ayanokouji kun   is that so  but you look like a really manly guy  ayanokouji kun  even though you re so slim  i could say that you re even better built than sudou  and he plays basketball","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.79, 87–88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Indoor swimming pool.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m really looking forward to this. Both Kouejin-kun and Sudou-kun are so fast,” (corpus renders Kōenji’s name as “Kouejin-kun” here — kept verbatim)<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? What’s the matter? Your face looks red for some reason. Are you not feeling well, by chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re much faster than average, too, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Races in the second girls&#x27; swimming heat; claims she wasn&#x27;t good at swimming in junior high, yet finishes second with a very respectable time of **approximately 31 seconds**.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands beside Ayanokōji by the pool deck in her school swimsuit; watches Kōenji and Sudō with genuine enthusiasm.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Observes Ayanokōji&#x27;s bare upper body with keen perception, looking at his muscular build with shock and awe.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? But you look like a really manly guy, Ayanokouji-kun. Even though you’re so slim, I could say that you’re even better built than Sudou, and he plays basketball.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Perceptive observation: first classmate to pierce Ayanokōji&#x27;s unassuming exterior and physically recognize his elite, hidden muscle development despite his deflections about &quot;good genes&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Casual, warm banter; notices his flushed nervousness and compliments his physique.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\">← Before: Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\">→ After: Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"cafe trap failure   the compulsion for 100  friendship classroom 1 d  outside dorms  then palate cafe in keyaki mall  palate cafe  kushida walks in  acting surprised  but horikita immediately exposes the four person table and nervous glances as a transparent setup   i ll just ask you outright  ayanokouji kun  have you seen horikita san smile even once   horikita san  whatever you say  i really want to be friends with you  when i saw you  i felt like it wasn t the first time we d met  i wondered if you felt the same way   it s okay  thank you  ayanokouji kun  it s true that i wasn t able to become her friend  but i was able to learn something important  that s enough for me   i wanted to be friends with everyone  not just the people in class d  but the students from other classes  too  but if i can t become friends with one girl in my class  then that means i ll never achieve my goal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.89, 91–93, 98–101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; outside dorms; then Palate Café in Keyaki Mall. Palate Café. Kushida walks in, acting surprised, but Horikita immediately exposes the four-person table and nervous glances as a transparent setup.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll just ask you outright. Ayanokouji-kun, have you seen Horikita-san smile even once?”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Horikita-san, whatever you say, I really want to be friends with you. When I saw you, I felt like it wasn’t the first time we’d met. I wondered if you felt the same way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s okay. Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. It’s true that I wasn’t able to become her friend, but…I was able to learn something important. That’s enough for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Smilingly invites Horikita to a café after class; when told not to invite her again because it&#x27;s a bother, Kushida maintains her bright grin and promises: *“I’ll invite you again.”*<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waits outside the dormitory for Ayanokōji. Takes his hand warmly, stepping into his personal space with a floral scent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Conspires with Ayanokōji to stage an ambush meeting disguised as coincidence at Palate Café in Keyaki Mall, directing him to lure Horikita there under the pretense of treating her to tea.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Faced with Horikita&#x27;s icy refusal to sit, Kushida mumbles an ominous hint of prior recognition.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita cuts her off, drops her bombshell about being alone for nine consecutive years, and leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kushida collapses silently into her seat, genuinely stunned and winded by the brutal rebuff.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Recovers her trademark sunshine smile in a split-second.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Moves to sit beside Ayanokōji at the table. When asked why she is so desperate to befriend Horikita when she already has more friends than anyone else, Kushida reveals her underlying psychological compulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to be friends with everyone. Not just the people in Class D, but the students from other classes, too. But if I can’t become friends with one girl in my class, then that means I’ll never achieve my goal…”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Terrifying emotional switch: can collapse in despair and snap back to a beaming smile in an instant; driven by an absolute, obsessive psychological need for 100% universal social acceptance—a single holdout (Horikita) invalidates her entire self-worth.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Suspects or hints at a prior encounter from junior high; fixated on conquering her wall.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deepens alliance; relies on him as a co-conspirator; surprised to learn he was also friendless in junior high.<span class=\"pg\">p.91, 100–101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\">← Before: Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\">→ After: Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"group outing   grounding yamauchi keyaki mall boutique and cafe   ha ha  i get the feeling ike kun is enjoying his time here to the fullest   do you mean you ll lose your sense of money management  yeah  that does sound pretty scary  actually   concurs with hirata that unearned wealth is dangerous   what about you  ayanokouji kun  do you think that 100 000 points is a lot or not enough   um  don t you mean the toeic  not apec","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.117–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Keyaki Mall boutique and café.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha! I get the feeling Ike-kun is enjoying his time here to the fullest!”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you mean you’ll lose your sense of money management? Yeah, that does sound pretty scary, actually.” (concurs with Hirata that unearned wealth is dangerous).<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What about you, Ayanokouji-kun? Do you think that 100,000 points is a lot or not enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Participates in the class shopping outing with Hirata, Karuizawa, Ike, Yamauchi, and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Yamauchi absurdly boasts that he scored 900 points on the &quot;APEC&quot;, Kushida gently and politely brings him back to reality without embarrassing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, don’t you mean the TOEIC, not APEC?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Socially unifying, attentive to everyone in the conversation, checks in on quiet members (Ayanokōji), defuses male boasting with gentle charm.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\">← Before: Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\">→ After: De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"de escalating violence   lending points without hesitation classroom 1 d  may 1st panic and lunch break   calm down  you two  okay  i m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we d be inspired to do better  right  besides  it s only been one month since we started here  right  like hirata kun said  it s better if we all do our best together  do you think that i m wrong about that   well  the teacher did say that the being late and talking in class were obviously bad  right   okay  sure   i can t just ignore a friend in need  karuizawa san has a lot of friends  too  so i think it s probably hard for her not to have any points   wait  how do you transfer points   this school really does take great care of its students  it even has a way to help students like karuizawa san   looks like the teacher wants to see you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.131–132, 134, 138–139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st panic and lunch break.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Calm down, you two, okay? I’m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we’d be inspired to do better, right?… Besides, it’s only been one month since we started here, right? Like Hirata-kun said, it’s better if we all do…”<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, the teacher did say that the being late and talking in class were obviously bad, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Okay, sure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps fearlessly between Yukimura and Hirata as Yukimura grabs Hirata&#x27;s collar; gently envelops Yukimura’s clenched fist with both hands to disarm his fury.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, you two, okay? I’m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we’d be inspired to do better, right?… Besides, it’s only been one month since we started here, right? Like Hirata-kun said, it’s better if we all do our best together. Do you think that I’m wrong about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Supreme emotional de-escalation: completely diffuses a physical altercation within seconds using gentle physical contact and moral appeal.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Verbally supports Hirata’s appeal from the podium when Sudō pushes back against rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Karuizawa casually hits her up for 2,000 private points to cover her deficit, Kushida agrees immediately without a shred of reluctance.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Explains her philosophy to Ayanokōji when he warns that she will likely never see those points returned.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t just ignore a friend in need. Karuizawa-san has a lot of friends, too, so I think it’s probably hard for her not to have any points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, how do you transfer points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school really does take great care of its students. It even has a way to help students like Karuizawa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Alerts Ayanokōji when the school PA summons him to the faculty office.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like the teacher wants to see you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pathological altruism / selfless facade: parts with her personal financial safety net instantly to preserve social harmony and project the perfect, supportive classmate persona.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Acts as an unconditional financial and emotional safety valve.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Integral co-mediator; provides the emotional anchor that backs up his structural leadership.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132, 134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\">← Before: Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\">→ After: Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"recruiting the failures   library study session hallway outside classroom 1 d  then school library   rejoice  kushida  you ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill  tomorrow  your hard work begins   ak to kushida   well  i do want to get closer to her  but  well  i won t worry about that now  besides  it s only natural to help out a friend in need   it s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade  isn t it awful to have to say goodbye after you ve worked to become friends with everyone  i ll do anything i can to be useful   ah  but there s just one thing i want to ask you  i want to participate in the study group  too  yes  i want to study with everyone   this might be too forward  but are you two already dating  it s a big rumor among the girls in our class  you know  they say that even though horikita san is always alone  she only seems to get along really well with you  ayanokouji kun  and you guys eat together  after all   horikita san  we re not going to be able to study with anyone if things continue like this   is it wrong  i don t want to abandon sudou kun  ike kun  and yamauchi kun   what  i don t understand  why do you say things like that  horikita san  why do you try to antagonize people  that s very sad","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.162–165, 173–175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hallway outside Classroom 1-D; then school library.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Rejoice, Kushida. You’ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill. Tomorrow, your hard work begins.” (AK to Kushida)<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I do want to get closer to her, but… well, I won’t worry about that now. Besides, it’s only natural to help out a friend in need.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade. Isn’t it awful to have to say goodbye after you’ve worked to become friends with everyone?… I’ll do anything I can to be useful!”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Approached by Ayanokōji after school; eagerly agrees to help gather Sudō, Ike, and Yamauchi for Horikita&#x27;s midterm study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grasps Ayanokōji&#x27;s hand warmly with an irresistible beaming smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sets her condition: insists that she also be allowed to participate in the study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, but there’s just one thing I want to ask you. I want to participate in the study group, too… Yes. I want to study with everyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks Ayanokōji point-blank if he and Horikita are dating, reporting widespread rumors among the girls that the solitary Horikita only opens up to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This might be too forward, but are you two already dating?… It’s a big rumor among the girls in our class, you know. They say that even though Horikita-san is always alone, she only seems to get along really well with you, Ayanokouji-kun. And you guys eat together, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Successfully secures Ayanokōji&#x27;s phone number.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Successfully mobilizes Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudō via text within hours using her feminine charm.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at the library wearing casual clothes; sits beside Horikita, brings snacks, and tries desperately to soothe the tension between Horikita and the failing boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Horikita declares the failing boys are &quot;dead weight&quot; better off expelled, Kushida is deeply distressed.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, we’re not going to be able to study with anyone if things continue like this…”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it wrong? I don’t want to abandon Sudou-kun, Ike-kun, and Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hurt and dismayed when Horikita accuses her of not genuinely caring about them; leaves the library resolved to find another way to save them.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? I don’t understand. Why do you say things like that, Horikita-san? Why do you try to antagonize people? That’s…very sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\">← Before: De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\">→ After: Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"rooftop unmasking   the sexual assault blackmail frame school rooftop and stairwell landing  dusk  around 6 00 pm   ahhh  so annoying   she s seriously annoying  god  how irritating  it d be better if she just died   ugh  i hate stuck up  snobby girls who think they re so cute  why is she such a harpy  a rotten girl like her couldn t possibly tutor me   ah  she s the worst  she s just the worst  the worst  the worst  horikita  you re so annoying  you re so damn annoying   what are you doing here   did you hear   if you tell anyone what you just heard  i won t forgive you   her words were ice   not an idle threat   in that case  i would tell everyone that you raped me  she said   that s okay  it wouldn t be false   her words had heft and power  leaving him unable to reply   your fingerprints are on my clothes  that s evidence of my claim  i m being serious  understand   i m going to leave this uniform in my room without washing it  if you betray me  i ll hand it over to the police   it s a promise  she said   steps away   that s none of your business   when ak asks which is the real her   is it bad to want everyone to like you  do you understand how difficult it is to accomplish that  you can t know  can you  she asked   at least on the surface  i wanted to appear to get along with horikita   yeah  that s what i want out of life  though  that way  my existence has meaning   answered without hesitation  her internal rules demand she get close to horikita   let me tell you somet","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.181–186<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School rooftop and stairwell landing, dusk (around 6:00 PM).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ahhh, so annoying!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s seriously annoying! God, how irritating. It’d be better if she just died…”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ugh, I hate stuck-up, snobby girls who think they’re so cute. Why is she such a harpy? A rotten girl like her couldn’t possibly tutor me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Believing herself completely alone on the locked rooftop, drops her sweet, angelic persona entirely. Viciously vents raw, murderous hatred toward Horikita Suzune in a harsh, guttural voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, she’s the worst! She’s just the worst, the worst, the worst! Horikita, you’re so annoying! You’re so damn annoying!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hears Ayanokōji accidentally kick the rooftop door; instantly freezes, turns, and locks onto him with a chilling, predatory glare.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What…are you…doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you hear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Marches down the stairs, places her left forearm against Ayanokōji’s throat, and pins him hard against the wall; her tone, her actions, everything about her completely unlike the Kushida he knew (her expression almost comparable to Horikita’s).<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you tell anyone what you just heard, I won’t forgive you.” (her words were ice — not an idle threat)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, I would tell everyone that you raped me,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s okay. It wouldn’t be false.” (her words had heft and power, leaving him unable to reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs his right wrist, slowly opens his hand, and pushes his palm up against her breast, holding it there despite his attempts to pull away.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your fingerprints are on my clothes. That’s evidence of my claim. I’m being serious. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to leave this uniform in my room without washing it. If you betray me, I’ll hand it over to the police.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s a promise,” she said. (steps away)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s none of your business.” (when AK asks which is the real her)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it bad to want everyone to like you? Do you understand how difficult it is to accomplish that? You can’t know, can you?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At least on the surface, I wanted to appear to get along with Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s what I want out of life, though. That way, my existence has meaning.” (answered without hesitation; her internal rules demand she get close to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me tell you something, while I have the chance. I absolutely despise gloomy, ordinary guys like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What the… I don’t know what you mean. Did Horikita-san say something about me?” she snapped. (when AK probes whether they knew each other before school)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just shut up. Hearing you talk irritates me, Ayanokouji-kun. I only want to know one thing. Do you swear you’ll never tell anyone what you learned here today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I believe you, Ayanokouji-kun.” (closes her eyes and slowly exhales)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, Ayanokouji-kun, you’re the only one that Horikita-san opens up to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After extracting his oath, the terrifying mask drops; she pivots smoothly into reflective analysis of Horikita as “the complete opposite” of herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Psychopathic dual personality / dark side: underneath the angelic, universally adored school idol lies a vicious, foul-mouthed sadist harboring burning hatred for anyone who rejects her (especially Horikita); chillingly pragmatic and capable of fabricating sexual assault charges with forensic precision to protect her secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Secret, venomous obsession and hatred; wishes she would die; considers her an unbearable, stuck-up harpy.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Traps him via manufactured sexual-assault evidence (fingerprints, unwashed uniform) and an unwinnable credibility contest; extracts a sworn oath, then reverts to warmth; establishes an uneasy, deadly truce.<span class=\"pg\">p.183–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\">← Before: Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\">→ After: Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"class a partnership  the ally test   the secret bond   you re free to think whatever you like  i just didn t want you to try to lie to me  i m glad you were honest  okay  i ll help  we re classmates  after all  right  ayanokouji kun   no  not for that  i want to work on getting into class a with you  i want to help with everything else you ll be doing   elevates her ask from study group helper to class a partner   really  yay   cheers  the three of them shake hands   her left and right arms extended to horikita and ak  plays along with ayanokoji s boyfriend bait by raising the stakes into a public motive   w well then  how about this  i ll go on a date with whoever scores highest on the test  i like people who work really hard  even when they don t like doing it   those girls are just being realists  you can t afford to eat on dreams alone   on the third year girls swarming kouenji   you re ranked a respectable fifth place in the hot guy rankings  congratulations  by the way  satonaka kun in class a is in first place  hirata kun s in second   relays the girls  anonymous ranking charts   talking to you is fun  ayanokouji kun     ha ha ha  yes  i did  hate you  sorry  but that s how i really feel   smiling  unrepentant   if horikita and i happen to clash  i hope that you ll cooperate with me  ayanokouji kun   first  we d need to build a relationship of mutual trust   declining to explain her situation until trust is established   don t you feel that a strange bond of mutual tru","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.204–217, 226, 233–235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re free to think whatever you like. I just didn’t want you to try to lie to me. I’m glad you were honest. Okay, I’ll help. We’re classmates, after all. Right, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, not for that. I want to work on getting into Class A with you. I want to help with everything else you’ll be doing.” (elevates her ask from study-group helper to Class A partner)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Really?! Yay!” (cheers; the three of them shake hands — her left and right arms extended to Horikita and AK)<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts Horikita&#x27;s unprecedented lunch invitation at Palate; probes her motive (&quot;Is it really for Sudou-kun and the others?&quot;) and is satisfied by the blunt selfish answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Immediately takes charge of luring the boys back; Ike and Yamauchi arrive visibly on cloud nine from her invitations.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Plays along with Ayanokōji&#x27;s boyfriend bait by raising the stakes into a public motive: “W-well then, how about this? I’ll go on a date with whoever scores highest on the test. I like people who work really hard, even when they don’t like doing it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waves Horikita off from across the room after ambushing AK into a lunch date — possibly engineered (&quot;Had she planned that, by chance?&quot;); keeps visible tabs on Ayanokōji post-rooftop.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those girls are just being realists. You can’t afford to eat on dreams alone.” (on the third-year girls swarming Kouenji)<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re ranked a respectable fifth place in the hot guy rankings. Congratulations! By the way, Satonaka-kun in Class A is in first place. Hirata-kun’s in second.” (relays the girls&#x27; anonymous ranking charts)<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Talking to you is fun, Ayanokouji-kun.” / “Ha ha ha, yes, I did [hate you]. Sorry, but that’s how I really feel.” (smiling, unrepentant)<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reveals the true purpose of the lunch: an alliance stress-test between herself and Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Horikita and I happen to clash, I hope that you’ll cooperate with me, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, we’d need to build a relationship of mutual trust.” (declining to explain her situation until trust is established)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts AK&#x27;s errand: broadcast Chabashira&#x27;s revised test-material list to all of Class D, including Hirata&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Co-conspirator on the old-test operation; agrees to take public credit as the receiver (&quot;from a third-year student you&#x27;re close to&quot;) so Ayanokōji stays invisible.<span class=\"pg\">p.233–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you feel that a strange bond of mutual trust forms between people who share a secret?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Honest-about-being-manipulative mode around AK: alliance ambition, candid roasts, and veiled threats delivered under an unbroken smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Secures conditional partnership with the Class A project — her biggest proximity gain to date.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Explicitly stakes a claim on his loyalty; wraps the old-test secret as mutual-trust bonding.<span class=\"pg\">p.216, 235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\">← Before: Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\">→ After: The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"the podium    i really hate you    actually  these are the old test problems  i got them from a third year student last night   the cover story lands perfectly   yes  to tell you the truth  i heard that the midterm test from the year before last had almost exactly the same problems as this one  so  if we study what s on this test  it ll surely come in handy   i just did it for my friends  it was nothing special   ha ha  you got me     that s right  i really hate you   do you want me to tell you the reason   offering the reason unprompted   refused","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.236–238<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Actually, these are the old test problems. I got them from a third-year student last night.” (the cover story lands perfectly)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. To tell you the truth, I heard that the midterm test from the year before last had almost exactly the same problems as this one. So, if we study what’s on this test, it’ll surely come in handy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I just did it for my friends. It was nothing special,”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the classroom podium the day before the exam to distribute the printed old-test sheets — the role neither Horikita nor AK could play; total class attention (even Sudou stops).<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Downplays her own role when Horikita praises her.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Cornered by Horikita&#x27;s direct &quot;You hate me, don&#x27;t you?&quot;, drops the pretense entirely and admits it with her smile intact.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha, you got me.” … “That’s right. I really hate you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you want me to tell you the reason?” (offering the reason unprompted — refused)<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Public-relations genius + weaponized honesty: delivers the class&#x27;s salvation from the podium while openly confirming hatred to her partner in the same afternoon.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The relationship&#x27;s true baseline established: confessed mutual hatred under a functioning alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\">← Before: Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: Relief at the results<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"relief at the results","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Relief at the results<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Shares a glance and sighs of relief with Ayanokōji at the posted results — until the red line appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\">← Before: The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: The Class A recruitment pitch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"the class a recruitment pitch   everything was thanks to horikita san s efforts  she tutored ike  yamauchi  and sudou   deflects credit onto horikita in front of the trio   we re all friends here  after all  horikita san  ayanokouji kun  and i are all working together to get into class a  if you re okay with it  i want you three to help us   yes  i absolutely am  increasing our points is an inevitable part of getting to the top as well  proverb war   a single arrow is easily broken  but not ten in a bundle    then  after horikita knocks the trio down   w well how about this  three heads are better than one  or something like that   if we keep going back and forth like this  though  we won t get anywhere  it s definitely better for us to get along   forces the truce that lands the recruits","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Class A recruitment pitch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256–261<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everything was thanks to Horikita-san’s efforts. She tutored Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudou.” (deflects credit onto Horikita in front of the trio)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’re all friends here, after all. Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun, and I are all working together to get into Class A. If you’re okay with it, I want you three to help us,”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. I absolutely am. Increasing our points is an inevitable part of getting to the top as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Praises Ayanokōji&#x27;s plain dorm room on request (&quot;It’s simple, but it feels nice and clean.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Escalates the gathering: reveals the Class A project to Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudou and formally recruits them as helpers.<span class=\"pg\">p.258–259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Proverb war: “A single arrow is easily broken, but not ten in a bundle,” — then, after Horikita knocks the trio down: “W-well how about this? Three heads are better than one! Or something like that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we keep going back and forth like this, though, we won’t get anywhere. It’s definitely better for us to get along.” (forces the truce that lands the recruits)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Morale engine: every time Horikita demoralizes the trio, Kushida rebuilds them — the recruitment pairing that makes the group functional.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\">← Before: Relief at the results<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 2  the social ceiling  narrated","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s snapshot of her position: &quot;She’s extremely popular and has many friends, both girls and boys. She gets in-person invitations, along with constant invites over the phone and through email... when she eats with friends she appears to have a real life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 3  group chat wistfulness kushida was the one who doubted horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite  kushida had doubted whether horikita would actually participate  since she hated talking with others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida was the one who doubted Horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite (&quot;Kushida had doubted whether Horikita would actually participate, since she hated talking with others.&quot;).<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  2 4  sudou s crisis conference   angel mode with an icy seam knocks during ak s kettle moment   kushida  the madonna of class d  poked her head through the entrance  she looked as cute as ever   oh  sudou kun s already here   yeah  i do  that s so we can meet up here  wait  did you not know about that  ayanokouji kun   she also holds a duplicate key to his room   assumed he d consented   umm  well should i return it to you   apologetically offers the key back   s suspended   oh  i got it  ayanokouji kun  he viciously beat chabashira sensei and then he spit on her   ha ha  i m only joking  sudou kun wouldn t go that far   the joke lands wrong   sudou s shock proves the secret is real   just wait a minute  sudou kun  can you please start over  and go a bit more slowly   a regular player  that s amazing  sudou kun  congratulations   still  that s amazing  we ve only just started school   so then they painted you as the bad guy  sudou kun   if class c started this  then sudou kun isn t at fault   we should tell chabashira sensei tomorrow  we should tell her it wasn t sudou kun s fault   sudou kun  you didn t lie to the teacher  did you  i mean  it seems strange  they didn t believe you even though you said you didn t do anything wrong  right   i guess that their plan is to severely punish sudou for punching them  huh   let s just come out and ask those three class c students to be honest  if they feel like what they did was wrong  then surely they d feel guilty about it  ri","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Knocks during AK&#x27;s kettle moment; &quot;Kushida, the Madonna of Class D, poked her head through the entrance. She looked as cute as ever.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Oh, Sudou-kun’s already here,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah, I do. That’s so we can meet up here… Wait, did you not know about that, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; (she also holds a duplicate key to his room — assumed he&#x27;d consented)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Umm, well…should I return it to you?&quot; (apologetically offers the key back)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;S-suspended?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, I got it, Ayanokouji-kun. He viciously beat Chabashira-sensei and then he spit on her!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha, I’m only joking! Sudou-kun wouldn’t go that far.&quot; (the joke lands wrong — Sudou&#x27;s shock proves the secret is real)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just wait a minute, Sudou-kun. Can you please start over, and go a bit more slowly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A regular player? That’s amazing, Sudou-kun! Congratulations!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Still, that’s amazing. We’ve only just started school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then they painted you as the bad guy, Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Class C started this, then Sudou-kun isn’t at fault.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should tell Chabashira-sensei tomorrow. We should tell her it wasn’t Sudou-kun’s fault,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, you didn’t lie to the teacher, did you? I mean, it seems strange. They didn’t believe you even though you said you didn’t do anything wrong. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess that their plan is to severely punish Sudou for punching them, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s just come out and ask those three Class C students to be honest. If they feel like what they did was wrong, then surely they’d feel guilty about it. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are two ways we can prove your innocence, Sudou-kun. The first way is to simply get those boys in Class C to admit that they lied. Since you weren’t at fault, it’s probably best to get them to acknowledge that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The other idea is to find the eyewitness you talked about, Sudou-kun. If someone happened to see the fight, then we should be able to get to the heart of the matter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Asking people one by one? Or we could simply address each class as a whole,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;H-huh? You don’t want us to tell anyone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But won’t the students in Class C talk about how Sudou-kun was violent? I mean, that would work in their favor, I’d think.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, I think it would be better if you kept your distance,&quot; (Sudou must stay away while accused)<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think it’s being dumped on us. We want you to rely on us, Sudou-kun. I don’t know how much we can do, but we’ll try our best. Okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a few things I wanted to talk to you about, Ayanokouji-kun. You didn’t seem very enthusiastic about helping Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Maybe, but Sudou-kun came to you, Ayanokouji-kun. He came to you before Horikita-san, Hirata-kun, or even Ike-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The mask slips mid-conversation: &quot;For an instant, Kushida’s glare turned icy, which perplexed me.&quot; — then she recomposes into advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think it might be better if you made more effort to blend in, Ayanokouji-kun,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. We’re friends. So what will you do, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think Horikita-san will help us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I know that you’re trying to dodge the question, but you’ll help, too. Won’t you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You won’t be useless. I’m sure you’ll be useful, somehow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So what should we do? Sudou-kun said that it wouldn’t help, but I think it’d be good to talk with the three students he fought. To tell you the truth, I’m friends with Komiya-kun and the others. Therefore, it might be possible to persuade them. Hmm, it may be dangerous, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, I guess looking for the eyewitness is our best bet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Structured empathy: jokes to defuse, then imposes an agenda (two proof routes), volunteers her cross-class network (Komiya et al. in C) as a tool, and pins AK to a commitment he keeps dodging.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her pressure only works socially — AK admits &quot;Like right now, I didn’t have the guts to promise that I’d help.&quot;; her icy glare is the only lever that lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Officially takes his side, secures his cooperation with warmth, keeps the secrecy bargain.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Escalates one-on-one after Sudou leaves; demands he publicly invest in the case; he internally recalls her &quot;I hate you&quot; warning while complying outwardly.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3 open  she takes the class s anger apart in front of everyone with the uproar starting to get out of hand  ak s note on her motive   naturally  kushida didn t want this to happen    she is defending the class s cohesion  not sudou  she tells the room sudou s whole account   the regular player nomination  the envious clubmates  the threat  the self defence   kushida conveyed yesterday s story to the whole class   everyone  can you please listen to what i have to say   what our teacher said seems to be true  sudou kun may have been in a fight  however  sudou kun was dragged into it   i d like to ask you all again  if anyone knows someone who saw what happened  whether it s someone in class  a friend  or an upperclassman  please tell me  you can contact me at any time  i would sincerely appreciate it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.41–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With the uproar starting to get out of hand, AK&#x27;s note on her motive: &quot;Naturally, Kushida didn’t want this to happen.&quot; — she is defending the class&#x27;s cohesion, not Sudou. She tells the room Sudou&#x27;s whole account — the regular-player nomination, the envious clubmates, the threat, the self-defence: &quot;Kushida conveyed yesterday’s story to the whole class.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, can you please listen to what I have to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What our teacher said seems to be true. Sudou-kun may have been in a fight. However, Sudou-kun was dragged into it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like to ask you all again. If anyone knows someone who saw what happened, whether it’s someone in class, a friend, or an upperclassman, please tell me. You can contact me at any time. I would sincerely appreciate it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK measures the difference between her and the teacher saying the same thing: &quot;Even though she’d basically said the same thing as Chabashira-sensei, the class had a very different response. She had an innate ability to connect with people. Her presence glowed so bright that I could almost feel it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Charisma alone does not carry it: after Yamauchi&#x27;s accusation, &quot;Kushida’s appeal for Sudou’s innocence didn’t seem to have reached anyone.&quot; It takes Hirata standing up — and then Karuizawa — to turn the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He backs her appeal publicly; AK credits the pair of them plus Karuizawa with converting the class, which is the closest the volume comes to the two leaders acting together.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> AK&#x27;s paired mechanism, stated in the same breath: &quot;If Kushida lived by the softness of her heart, then Karuizawa lived by the strength of her will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  3 1  keeping ayanokoji inside the group she assembles the lunch table   ak  horikita  ike  yamauchi  sudou   by asking him directly   when lunchtime came  kushida had invited me with a smile  she d said   want to get lunch  i d said okay  of course  i mean  i didn t have any choice in the matter  she leaves the table early to work her own network   ah  sorry  i have to go for a bit  i m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44, p.47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She assembles the lunch table — AK, Horikita, Ike, Yamauchi, Sudou — by asking him directly: &quot;When lunchtime came, Kushida had invited me with a smile. She’d said, &#x27;Want to get lunch?&#x27; I’d said okay, of course. I mean, I didn’t have any choice in the matter.&quot; She leaves the table early to work her own network: “Ah, sorry. I have to go for a bit. I’m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything.”<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 3  3 2 3 3  horikita  the lesson  and class b she takes ak s arm in front of ike and yamauchi and walks him out with her  ike and yamauchi are left behind because  as ak notes   you certainly couldn t claim those two were friendly with horikita  in the class b room she is the only one of the four who moves   kushida was the only one who remained unfazed  in fact  she found her class b friends and  with a smile on her face  waved to them and headed over  she pitches sudou s case to the roughly ten class b students still in the room   the first cross class advocacy of the volume   are you really heading back  horikita san   you will help us out  won t you   stopping ak from slipping out  ak   i couldn t refuse  slightly upturned eyes   pleading   lethal   i want to get horikita san to help us out this time  can you try asking her again   yeah  i want to chase after her  if horikita san helps  i think she ll make a big difference   i really want you to help us with sudou s case  is that possible   i know you did  but but  i think this is necessary to reach class a   w wait  what do you mean  wasn t sudou kun dragged into the fight   sudou kun is a perpetrator  is that true   i don t agree with abandoning sudou kun just to punish him  if she s dissatisfied with him  i think she should at least talk to him directly  that s what friends would do   okay  i understand  i ll follow your advice  ayanokouji kun   no  i m sorry  i failed   well then  let s go to class b right away   i","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes AK&#x27;s arm in front of Ike and Yamauchi and walks him out with her; Ike and Yamauchi are left behind because, as AK notes, &quot;You certainly couldn’t claim those two were friendly with Horikita.&quot; In the Class B room she is the only one of the four who moves: &quot;Kushida was the only one who remained unfazed. In fact, she found her Class B friends and, with a smile on her face, waved to them and headed over.&quot; She pitches Sudou&#x27;s case to the roughly ten Class B students still in the room — the first cross-class advocacy of the volume.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you really heading back? Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You will…help us out, won’t you?” (stopping AK from slipping out; AK: &quot;I couldn’t refuse. Slightly upturned eyes + pleading = lethal.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to get Horikita-san to help us out this time. Can you try asking her again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I want to chase after her. If Horikita-san helps, I think she’ll make a big difference.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really want you to help us with Sudou’s case. Is that possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you did, but…but, I think this is necessary to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait. What do you mean? Wasn’t Sudou-kun dragged into the fight?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun is a perpetrator? Is that…true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t agree with abandoning Sudou-kun just to punish him. If she’s dissatisfied with him, I think she should at least talk to him directly. That’s what friends would do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I understand. I’ll follow your advice, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s definition of her, offered as a limit on himself: &quot;She would extend her hand to a friend in need as many times as it took. It sounds simple, but it was actually difficult. Only someone like Kushida could do such a thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is moved mid-conversation and lets it show: &quot;Kushida arched her back and stretched; I’d changed her thinking.&quot; — then converts the new position into action (&quot;Okay, let’s go hunt for the witness.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m sorry. I failed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, let’s go to Class B right away!”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also think you’re being too negative. I do think it’s a good idea to ask Class B, but I also think we should ask several people at once. If not, we may not find the witness in time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, Ayanokouji-kun.” (overruling his one-at-a-time plan with Ike and Yamauchi behind her, and apologising for it; AK withdraws: &quot;Kushida’s plan had convinced me, so I withdrew my own.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s note on the transferability of her manner: &quot;She chatted with people regardless of gender, exactly how she acted in Class D. No one was more jealous of this than Ike and Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her network has a ceiling she cannot see: AK&#x27;s whole plan for Class B rests on the class&#x27;s self-interest, and she is running on friendship, which is why the report she brings back surprises him. (What the report is, the text withholds until the next chapter.)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 0 4 1  she runs the search  and is the only one who can name sakura s seat horikita arrives at the room and kushida is the reason she stays   kushida peered over at the entrance  probably concerned that horikita wouldn t return   ah  horikita san  kushida said  kushida smiled and waved to horikita  she is the class s map of itself   no  you re both wrong  she sits diagonally ahead of sudou kun to the right    ak   kushida corrected them  a slightly pouty look on her face   as long as we can find a witness  it s not impossible  let s keep trying our best  ike kun    the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless  she re engineers the search from the witness to the witness s surroundings   we might want to change our methods a little  for example  let s look for someone who might have found a witness    ak s judgement   that wasn t a bad idea   if you didn t come here to help  then why did you come    and then  instead of pressing   well  i m happy if you just want to listen to us talk  i hoped you could give some advice  she defends a classmate she has never spoken to  in public  against ike   it s not good to remember people based on something like that  ikekun  that s pathetic  the phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing   no luck  the call didn t go through  i can try again later  but this may be a delicate matter  and  she gave me her contact information  but she doesn t know me very well  she might be confused if i trie","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita arrives at the room and Kushida is the reason she stays: &quot;Kushida peered over at the entrance, probably concerned that Horikita wouldn’t return. &#x27;Ah, Horikita-san!&#x27; Kushida said. Kushida smiled and waved to Horikita.&quot; She is the class&#x27;s map of itself: &quot;No, you’re both wrong. She sits diagonally ahead of Sudou-kun to the right.&quot; — AK: &quot;Kushida corrected them, a slightly pouty look on her face.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As long as we can find a witness, it’s not impossible. Let’s keep trying our best, Ike-kun.&quot; — the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad…<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you didn’t come here to help, then why did you come?&quot; — and then, instead of pressing: &quot;Well, I’m happy if you just want to listen to us talk. I hoped you could give some advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her method of remembering is exact: &quot;It’s certainly true that Sudou-kun didn’t say he saw anyone. He said that he had a feeling that someone was there.&quot; — she corrects the class&#x27;s summary of a claim three days old.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She defends a classmate she has never spoken to, in public, against Ike: &quot;It’s not good to remember people based on something like that, Ikekun! That’s pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing: &quot;No luck. The call didn’t go through. I can try again later, but this may be a delicate matter.&quot; and &quot;She gave me her contact information, but she doesn’t know me very well. She might be confused if I tried to call her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She reads the room&#x27;s failure before it happens and shrinks the plan to one person: &quot;Well, I’ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow. I think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She holds Sakura&#x27;s number and Sakura&#x27;s seating position and none of Sakura&#x27;s trust, and is the one student whose name she will not let Ike reduce to a body.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 2 4 3  the approach fails in front of the whole class  class was over  kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards sakura  who was quietly preparing to leave  kushida seemed oddly nervous  she takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers   i i m sorry  it s because i came up and talked to you so suddenly  that    and is answered flatly   no  that s not it  i was just careless  that s all  anyway  goodbye   sakura san  then  i wanted to ask you something  sakura san  do you have a moment  it s about sudou s case   can you please make some time  this is important  so i d like to talk to you  when sudou kun was involved in the incident  were you perhaps somewhere nearby   can t you please spare just a few minutes now    the third ask  the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.86–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Class was over. Kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards Sakura, who was quietly preparing to leave. Kushida seemed oddly nervous.&quot; She takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers: &quot;I-I’m sorry. It’s because I came up and talked to you so suddenly, that…&quot; — and is answered flatly: &quot;No, that’s not it. I was just careless, that’s all… Anyway, goodbye.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura-san?&quot; then &quot;I wanted to ask you something, Sakura-san. Do you have a moment? It’s about Sudou’s case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can you please make some time? This is important, so I’d like to talk to you. When Sudou-kun was involved in the incident, were you perhaps somewhere nearby?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can’t you please spare just a few minutes now?&quot; — the third ask, the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> AK&#x27;s post-mortem of her judgement, in her own terms: &quot;Kushida probably had expected this conversation to go more smoothly, and had gone into this situation thinking she wasn’t going to be rejected. That explained why this was currently falling apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Even after failing she keeps the case alive by asking the quietest boy in the room: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you’re Sudou-kun’s ally, aren’t you?&quot; — &quot;Well, it’s just that things seem to a bit tense. Everyone’s desire to save Sudou is fading.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She uses his proximity as a resource twice in one day: the ally question, and the earlier instruction that he keep Horikita reachable (Hirata briefs AK about her because &quot;she doesn’t talk to anyone except for you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 8  she phones him at night  and cannot finish what she starts the first time she reaches him unbidden  after ten   i m sorry for calling you so late  you re still up  she asked   sakura san s digital camera was broken  right  i feel like i m partially to blame since i made her so flustered  so i wanted to take responsibility for that   yeah  she seemed hesitant at first  but then said that she d be fine with the day after tomorrow  i think that sakura s digital camera is probably really important to her   if we were just going to get it repaired  i suppose  but  there s another thing  i d like your help with it  ayanokouji kun  what horikita has concluded  carried by the one person horikita will not speak to   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  after getting a bit closer to sakura san  i also think she knows something  but there has to be some reason why she s keeping quiet  since she keeps denying that she witnessed it   that reminds me  it was really scary when kouenji kun and sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting    printed as one word  kept as the translation has it   i couldn t even move  hirata kun was so amazing  though   class d was able to come together  thanks to you and hirata  the fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part  too   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.128–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first time she reaches him unbidden, after ten: &quot;I’m sorry for calling you so late. You’re still up?&quot; she asked.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura-san’s digital camera was broken, right? I feel like I’m partially to blame since I made her so flustered. So I wanted to take responsibility for that…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. She seemed hesitant at first, but then said that she’d be fine with the day after tomorrow. I think that Sakura’s digital camera is probably really important to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If we were just going to get it repaired, I suppose. But, there’s another thing. I’d like your help with it, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> What Horikita has concluded, carried by the one person Horikita will not speak to: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything. After getting a bit closer to Sakura-san, I also think she knows something. But there has to be some reason why she’s keeping quiet, since she keeps denying that she witnessed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That reminds me. It was really scary when Kouenji-kun and Sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting.&quot; — printed as one word; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata. The fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? Ah, yeah, it is. Why? What about it?&quot; — he has asked whether her room is on the ninth floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her gift with the class&#x27;s outliers, described from the outside: &quot;Kushida had done a wonderful job taking the proper first steps to earn Sakura’s trust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The only silence the volume records her in: &quot;Suddenly, Kushida fell silent. It was unexpected silence, without warning. Our conversation, which had been smooth up until now, came to a screeching halt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She starts a confession three times and stops: &quot;Hey—&quot; then &quot;I-If… Well… I… I—&quot; then &quot;No, it’s nothing.&quot; — and the recorder&#x27;s verdict: &quot;That sure didn’t seem like nothing…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’ll see you the day after tomorrow, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — the call&#x27;s last line, with the unfinished one still in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only classmate who tests his account of Horikita instead of accepting it — and his reaction to being read is discomfort rather than deflection: &quot;I didn’t like being misunderstood by Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130–131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She hesitates immediately after being asked for her floor number, and the volume never says whether the two are connected. What is recorded is only the sequence: the question, the halt, the swallowed sentence, the goodbye.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 9 4 10  how she works on someone who cannot be worked on   good morning  and  sorry  were you waiting long   this is the first time we ve met up on a day off  it s refreshing  the opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class   weren t you really busy during your downtime last week  i m glad that you came despite that  ayanokouji kun    then  precisely   i m talking about ike kun and the others going to that cafe  of course   by any chance   i didn t mean anything  i m sorry  i guess i said something wrong    and when he says he does not care   you do seem to care   no  no  that s not true at all  i think we re great together    to his  i think i might look a little out of place next to you   you re that surprisingly delicate  ayanokouji kun  i don t really care what others say  i don t think it s an insult at all  i really think we suit each other   she asked me to invite you  ayanokouji kun  didn t sakura san contact you    sakura s invitation came through kushida  and kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly   right now  how about we sit and wait   let s see  i m sure they have a repair counter somewhere  let s check it out   there it is  the repairs counter   what s the matter  sakura san    she is the only one of the three who asks about sakura s fear out loud   that clerk sure was something else  he talked with such incredible passion  i was just so shocked   n no  i wasn t disgusted by him  do you know something  about that cler","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning!&quot; and &quot;Sorry. Were you waiting long?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is the first time we’ve met up on a day off. It’s refreshing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and…<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and the others going to that café, of course.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;By any chance…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn’t mean anything… I’m sorry, I guess I said something wrong…&quot; — and when he says he does not care: &quot;You do seem to care…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, no, that’s not true at all. I think we’re great together,&quot; — to his &quot;I think I might look a little out of place next to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re that surprisingly delicate, Ayanokouji-kun? I don’t really care what others say. I don’t think it’s an insult at all. I really think we suit each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She asked me to invite you, Ayanokouji-kun. Didn’t Sakura-san contact you?&quot; — Sakura&#x27;s invitation came through Kushida, and Kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Right now, how about we sit and wait?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s see, I’m sure they have a repair counter somewhere. Let’s check it out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There it is! The repairs counter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s the matter, Sakura-san?&quot; — she is the only one of the three who asks about Sakura&#x27;s fear out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The transaction as an act of translation: &quot;Kushida’s worldly wisdom was certainly impressive. Even though it was her first time meeting the store clerk, she was soon talking to him as if they were longtime friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She reads the clerk&#x27;s interest and manages it without refusing him: &quot;In order to conclude their business, she urged Sakura to hand over the camera.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That clerk sure was something else. He talked with such incredible passion, I was just so shocked,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, I wasn’t disgusted by him. Do you know something? About that clerk?&quot; — the question that lets Sakura say she was afraid.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you know about this, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; — &quot;Kushida seemed to have an epiphany. She turned to me with wide eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You really looked out for Sakura-san,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no need to thank me.&quot; and then &quot;Sakura-san, you really like your camera. Don’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think being knowledgeable and liking things are separate matters. It’s wonderful to be so passionate about something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, have we met somewhere before?&quot; — &quot;Kushida murmured.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that Sakura refuses: &quot;Sorry. It’s just that when I look at you, I get this feeling that we’ve met before, Sakura-san. Hey, weird question, but could you try removing your glasses?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should hang out together again, Sakura-san. Not just with me, but with my other friends, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her offer of a normal relationship, phrased as a complaint about speech: &quot;you can talk to us normally, you know? If it’s okay with you. We’re in the same grade. It sounds a little weird when you speak so formally to us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s not really a bad thing! I mean, I’d be happy if you didn’t speak so formally to me, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s okay, though. You don’t need to force yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that finally gets the witness: &quot;So, does that mean that you saw Sudou-kun fight with those other students?&quot; and then &quot;No, we do. Why did you decide to tell us now, though? I mean, I’m happy you did, but I don’t want you to force yourself. You don’t have to do this just because you’re grateful, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that really true? You’re not forcing yourself?&quot; Kushida asked. — the same question twice in one minute, because the first answer was a shake of the head.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san. I’m sure Sudou-kun will be really happy.&quot; — &quot;Kushida took Sakura’s hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The case the whole class failed to move in three weeks is closed by a hand-hold and two refusals to press: &quot;I wondered if a new friendship had been born right here, right now. At any rate, we had Sudou’s witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only person in Class D who gets things done by being with people rather than by being right about them; the volume records her succeeding at exactly the task Horikita wrote off as worthless.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> From a camera knocked over in a classroom (p.90) to a promise to testify in a shopping mall: the whole distance is crossed by Kushida refusing to make anything harder than it already is.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She recruits him by asking, tests whether he has been left out of his own friend group, and lets him fill in a form; he is her one witness that she is capable of a plain conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her instinct to close on Sakura stops short of the truth: she asks about the glasses, gets refused, and &quot;Kushida seemed to feel that it would make trouble if she pressed the issue, so she kept quiet. Or rather, she didn’t ask anything else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 4  4 11  the same evening  on two calls   we got closer to sakura  but  is it really okay for me to say that    her voice on the phone that night  the translation leaves the reply s speaker untagged and it is not assigned  her reason for the glasses  which turns out not to be a reason   well  i mean  i thought saying so might be kind of cruel  but  i just feel like her glasses don t really suit her  for some reason  it s like she doesn t really need them  or something  i don t understand it myself  i also thought that we d met somewhere before  but that was probably just a misunderstanding   huh  sakura san wears fake glasses  but she said that her eyesight was really bad   appearing fashionable with glasses  hmm  that doesn t sound normal   there s that  wearing glasses does make you look smart   i knew it was right to bring you along  ayanokouji kun  i feel like you re very observant of people   oh  sure  sorry for talking so long    the line she says when he cuts her off to answer sakura   though there was a heavy regret in those parting words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.147–150<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We got closer to Sakura, but… Is it really okay for me to say that?&quot; — her voice on the phone that night; the translation leaves the reply&#x27;s speaker untagged and it is not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really…<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Huh? Sakura-san wears fake glasses? But she said that her eyesight was really bad…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really need them, or something. I don’t understand it myself. I also thought that we’d met somewhere before, but that was probably just a misunderstanding.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Appearing fashionable with glasses? Hmm, that doesn’t sound normal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s that. Wearing glasses does make you look smart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I knew it was right to bring you along, Ayanokouji-kun. I feel like you’re very observant of people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, sure. Sorry for talking so long.&quot; — the line she says when he cuts her off to answer Sakura; &quot;Though there was a heavy regret in those parting words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is asked whether Sakura called her and did not receive the call: &quot;A few minutes later, Kushida confirmed that she hadn’t heard back from Sakura.&quot; The volume leaves Sakura&#x27;s unfinished sentence on one side of the exchange and Kushida&#x27;s unfinished sentence on the other.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 5  5 1  she reads horikita better than horikita reads herself she does not come in  she  briefly peeked into the classroom  and calls him out to the hallway   good morning  ayanokouji kun   thanks for yesterday  you really saved me   let s hang out again sometime  okay   i have a feeling i just saw something really incredible   that s not it  i think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited   she probably doesn t know how she feels  i m sure she s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them  though  that s a good thing  a good thing   perhaps you re realizing something fundamental  ayanokouji kun  horikita san is upset that you didn t invite her to come along","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She does not come in; she &quot;briefly peeked into the classroom&quot; and calls him out to the hallway.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning! Ayanokouji-kun!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Thanks for yesterday. You really saved me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Let’s hang out again sometime, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a feeling I just saw something really incredible!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not it. I think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She probably doesn’t know how she feels… I’m sure she’s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them, though. That’s a good thing, a good thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps you’re realizing something fundamental, Ayanokouji-kun. Horikita-san is upset that you didn’t invite her to come along.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The reading is hers alone; the narrator calls it &quot;a bizarre thought&quot; and cannot accept it.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She names Horikita&#x27;s feeling as loneliness while disliking her, and says it in the hallway where Horikita cannot hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  she brings the witness  then loses the seat lunch in the classroom   thanks to kushida s persuasive tears  horikita joins the strategy meeting  mid argument she stops listening   kushida  seated beside me as the ike yamauchi spectacle unfolded  appeared deep in thought   yes  sakura san saw everything from start to finish   sensei  sakura san is    cut off   chabashira sensei cut kushida off sharply   chabashira sensei  that s a horrible thing to say   do you mind if we participate as well  sensei   can we really prove sudou s innocence tomorrow   perhaps    murmured  then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it   ah  nothing  it s nothing  there was just something on my mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–168<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch in the classroom; &quot;thanks to Kushida’s persuasive tears&quot; Horikita joins the strategy meeting. Mid-argument she stops listening: &quot;Kushida, seated beside me as the Ike/Yamauchi spectacle unfolded, appeared deep in thought.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. Sakura-san saw everything from start to finish.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sensei, Sakura-san is…&quot; — cut off: &quot;Chabashira-sensei cut Kushida off sharply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Chabashira-sensei, that’s a horrible thing to say!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> &quot;Kushida called for Sakura, who stood quietly behind her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you mind if we participate as well, sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Of course, it was Kushida who spoke up, most likely to support Sakura.&quot; — she asks for a place and Horikita takes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can we really prove Sudou’s innocence tomorrow?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps…&quot; — murmured, then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, nothing. It’s nothing. There was just something on my mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 5  5 6  the idol  the persona theory  and the whisper at the door that night  under kushida s orders  everyone but sudo gathers in ayanokoji s room  she asks for his computer and opens a blog   there has been progress  yes  but i ve also noticed something incredible  ayanokouji kun  can i borrow your computer for a minute   okay  have a look at this   do you recognize her   look closely   no  not that  this is sakura san  isn t it   sakura san  from our class   when i saw ike kun reading that weekly magazine  i remembered something  i had the feeling i d seen sakura somewhere before   but just when shizuku started to become really popular  she suddenly disappeared   i was surprised when i found out that she was an idol  but i also kind of understood it  i wonder if that s her real personality   i ll tell you later  right now  our priority is to resolve this case  besides  it s a personal request   i m sorry  if i told you now  it d just be a bother   if you listen to my request  ayanokouji kun i ll give you my most precious possession    whispered at the door  on tiptoe  hand on his chest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">That night &quot;under Kushida’s orders&quot; everyone but Sudō gathers in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room; she asks for his computer and opens a blog.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There has been progress, yes, but I’ve also noticed something incredible. Ayanokouji-kun, can I borrow your computer for a minute?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Okay. Have a look at this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reveal&#x27;s opening exchange is untagged: &quot;Wait, is that a picture of Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;She’s a gravure idol. She was just featured in a young men’s magazine.&quot; — only the next question, &quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;, carries her name.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Look closely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, not that! This is Sakura-san, isn’t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, from our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When I saw Ike-kun reading that weekly magazine, I remembered something. I had the feeling I’d seen Sakura somewhere before,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But just when Shizuku started to become really popular, she suddenly disappeared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was surprised when I found out that she was an idol, but I also kind of understood it. I wonder if that’s her real personality?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her theory of the double life: &quot;I think that…most likely, Sakura-san would say that her idol self is actually her false face.&quot; then &quot;I think that she’s creating another personality with makeup.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll tell you later. Right now, our priority is to resolve this case. Besides, it’s a personal request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry. If I told you now, it’d just be a bother.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you listen to my request, Ayanokouji-kun…I’ll give you my most precious possession.&quot; — whispered at the door, on tiptoe, hand on his chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> By the time the door opens the change is gone: &quot;Not even the faintest trace of that frightening Kushida remained.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She turns the request into a transaction before she has named it.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 6 open  the send off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her only spoken line in the chapter is the room’s send-off to the two people going into the hearing — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — and Horikita does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She gives the encouragement to both of them together, including the girl who has spent the volume refusing her, and the page records no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 6  6 2  named among the people who believe sakura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Ayanokōji tells Sakura that the belief is not his alone — &quot;Horikita, Kushida, and Sudou do, too. All of our classmates believe you.&quot; Her part is reported by him, not shown in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 7  her email  and the reward still to come","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.225–246<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji states that he asked her to send the email that lured the three Class C students to the special building: &quot;I asked her to send an email to compel you all to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita lists her hearing actions among those that &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  the first name permission  the leader nomination  and the shared meal deck of the liner  the extraordinary view  had stolen her breath away","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the first-name permission, the leader nomination, and the shared meal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.14–20, p.66–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the extraordinary view &quot;had stolen her breath away.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ibuki-mio\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Grants Ike first-name permission and offers &quot;Kanjikun&quot; in return — the exchange that sets Ike&#x27;s confession plan running.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present when Sudou fumbles Horikita&#x27;s first name as Tomiko; the correction to Suzune lands in front of the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Nominates Horikita as spot-leader in the circle — Hirata and Karuizawa &quot;stand out too much,&quot; but responsibility is the criterion: &quot;I think that Horikita-san meets that criteria.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji reads the nomination as the least-risk play: Horikita &quot;was so desperate to reach Class A. That was crucial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Walks over with a meal seat and water from her own group&#x27;s ration — four people sharing three portions — while Ibuki protests &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;Kushida, who wished for everyone’s happiness, had charity to spare.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Raises her hand for river water once the vote is already tipping, which Ayanokōji suspects is influence rather than conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"}];
